1
00:00:02,294 --> 00:00:04,087
OKAY, SHE IS THE STAR
OF THE PLAY

2
00:00:04,129 --> 00:00:05,589
AND SHE IS
MY GIRLFRIEND.

3
00:00:05,631 --> 00:00:06,924
I GET TO HAVE SEX

4
00:00:06,966 --> 00:00:08,425
WITH THE STAR
OF THE PLAY.

5
00:00:08,467 --> 00:00:11,094
PEOPLE CAN HEAR YOU.

6
00:00:11,136 --> 00:00:12,972
I KNOW!

7
00:00:20,061 --> 00:00:22,105
WOW, SHE LOOKS GREAT,
DOESN'T SHE?

8
00:00:22,147 --> 00:00:24,525
( grunts )

9
00:00:24,566 --> 00:00:25,985
Man:
HI.

10
00:00:26,025 --> 00:00:29,613
THAT IS ONE
GOOD-LOOKING MAN.

11
00:00:29,655 --> 00:00:31,281
IS IT JUST ME

12
00:00:31,323 --> 00:00:33,367
OR CAN YOU ACTUALLY
SEE HIS ABS

13
00:00:33,408 --> 00:00:35,953
THROUGH HIS OVERCOAT?

14
00:00:35,995 --> 00:00:39,623
Man:
SO, YOU BEEN DOING THIS LONG?

15
00:00:39,665 --> 00:00:41,625
Kathy:
NO, YOU'RE MY FIRST.

16
00:00:41,667 --> 00:00:44,043
PUT THE MONEY ON THE TABLE.

17
00:00:45,587 --> 00:00:47,130
( passionate moaning )

18
00:00:47,172 --> 00:00:49,633
Man:
OH, YEAH, OH, YEAH,
THAT'S NICE.

19
00:00:49,675 --> 00:00:52,011
( moaning continues )

20
00:00:52,051 --> 00:00:53,595
DUDE.

21
00:00:56,181 --> 00:00:59,059
Man:
IS THAT AN EXPENSIVE BLOUSE?

22
00:00:59,100 --> 00:01:00,644
Kathy:
IF YOU WANT IT TO BE.

23
00:01:00,686 --> 00:01:02,062
( fabric ripping )

24
00:01:02,103 --> 00:01:03,689
Kathy:
OH!

25
00:01:05,440 --> 00:01:07,776
HERE'S YOUR
GIRLFRIEND'S BUTTON.

26
00:01:15,283 --> 00:01:20,039
♪ SO NO ONE TOLD YOU
LIFE WAS GONNA BE THIS WAY ♪

27
00:01:20,080 --> 00:01:22,541
♪ YOUR JOB'S A JOKE,
YOU'RE BROKE ♪

28
00:01:22,583 --> 00:01:24,919
♪ YOUR LOVE LIFE'S D.O.A. ♪

29
00:01:24,960 --> 00:01:28,839
♪ IT'S LIKE YOU'RE ALWAYS
STUCK IN SECOND GEAR ♪

30
00:01:28,881 --> 00:01:31,466
♪ WHEN IT HASN'T BEEN YOUR DAY ♪

31
00:01:31,508 --> 00:01:35,136
♪ YOUR WEEK, YOUR MONTH,
OR EVEN YOUR YEAR ♪

32
00:01:35,178 --> 00:01:38,974
♪ BUT I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

33
00:01:39,016 --> 00:01:41,268
♪ WHEN THE RAIN
STARTS TO POUR ♪

34
00:01:41,309 --> 00:01:44,021
♪ I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

35
00:01:44,063 --> 00:01:46,648
♪ LIKE I'VE BEEN THERE BEFORE ♪

36
00:01:46,690 --> 00:01:48,525
♪ I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

37
00:01:48,567 --> 00:01:54,740
♪ 'CAUSE YOU'RE THERE
FOR ME, TOO. ♪

38
00:01:58,953 --> 00:02:00,662
OH, HEY, MON,
DO YOU STILL HAVE

39
00:02:00,704 --> 00:02:04,291
YOUR OLD BLOUSES AND DRESSES
FROM HIGH SCHOOL?

40
00:02:04,332 --> 00:02:07,419
YEAH, I THINK I HAVE SOME
AROUND HERE SOMEWHERE. WHY?

41
00:02:07,461 --> 00:02:09,797
IT'S JUST MATERNITY CLOTHES
ARE SO EXPENSIVE.

42
00:02:11,548 --> 00:02:13,675
Monica:
RACH, I MADE
A PILE OF YOUR STUFF

43
00:02:13,717 --> 00:02:15,176
ON THIS SIDE
OF THE ROOM.

44
00:02:15,218 --> 00:02:16,470
IF YOU COULD JUST...

45
00:02:16,511 --> 00:02:18,179
( grunts )

46
00:02:18,221 --> 00:02:20,432
THROW YOUR PURSES AT IT?

47
00:02:20,474 --> 00:02:23,310
BLOOMINGDALE'S ELIMINATED
MY DEPARTMENT.

48
00:02:23,351 --> 00:02:24,269
( gasps )

49
00:02:24,311 --> 00:02:25,729
GOD! ARE YOU OUT
OF A JOB?

50
00:02:25,771 --> 00:02:28,273
NO, BUT THEY STUCK ME
IN PERSONAL SHOPPING

51
00:02:28,315 --> 00:02:30,609
WHICH IS JUST
A HUGE STEP DOWN.

52
00:02:30,651 --> 00:02:32,402
"PERSONAL SHOPPING"--
WHAT IS THAT?

53
00:02:32,444 --> 00:02:34,905
LIKE, WHERE WALK AROUND
WITH SNOOTY RICH PEOPLE

54
00:02:34,947 --> 00:02:36,323
AND TELL THEM WHAT TO BUY?

55
00:02:36,364 --> 00:02:37,282
UH-HUH.

56
00:02:37,324 --> 00:02:39,785
THAT SOUNDS GREAT.

57
00:02:39,827 --> 00:02:42,579
HEY.

58
00:02:42,621 --> 00:02:43,831
UM... EXCUSE ME.

59
00:02:43,872 --> 00:02:45,332
WE SWITCHED APARTMENTS.

60
00:02:45,373 --> 00:02:47,292
YOU CAN'T EAT OUR FOOD ANYMORE.

61
00:02:47,334 --> 00:02:48,961
THAT GRAVY TRAIN HAS ENDED.

62
00:02:49,003 --> 00:02:50,629
THERE'S GRAVY?

63
00:02:52,131 --> 00:02:53,715
IF YOU HAVE THE BIG APARTMENT

64
00:02:53,757 --> 00:02:56,510
YOU HAVE TO DEAL WITH PEOPLE
COMING OVER ALL THE TIME.

65
00:02:56,551 --> 00:02:58,637
THAT FRIDGE HAS GOT
TO BE STOCKED, OKAY?

66
00:03:02,474 --> 00:03:03,684
WHAT ARE YOU DOING?

67
00:03:03,725 --> 00:03:06,061
I THINK I LEFT
A DONUT UP HERE.

68
00:03:09,731 --> 00:03:10,858
HEY.

69
00:03:10,899 --> 00:03:11,984
HEY.
HEY.

70
00:03:12,026 --> 00:03:14,235
OH, HOW WAS
KATHY'S PLAY?

71
00:03:14,277 --> 00:03:16,864
WELL, KATHY GETS HALF-NAKED
AND SIMULATES SEX

72
00:03:16,905 --> 00:03:19,992
WITH A REAL
GOOD-LOOKING GUY.

73
00:03:20,034 --> 00:03:23,244
IT WAS LIKE SOMEBODY LITERALLY
WROTE DOWN MY WORST NIGHTMARE

74
00:03:23,286 --> 00:03:25,998
AND THEN CHARGED ME
$32 TO SEE IT.

75
00:03:26,040 --> 00:03:29,292
THAT'S A GOOD IDEA
FOR A BUSINESS.

76
00:03:29,334 --> 00:03:30,836
I'M TOTALLY SCREWED, OKAY?

77
00:03:30,878 --> 00:03:32,671
THEY'RE GOING TO BE
HOT AND HEAVY

78
00:03:32,713 --> 00:03:34,048
ON STAGE EVERY NIGHT

79
00:03:34,089 --> 00:03:36,299
AND THEY'RE GOING TO GO
TO THEIR CAST PARTIES

80
00:03:36,341 --> 00:03:37,968
AND HE'LL TRY TO UNDERMINE ME.

81
00:03:38,010 --> 00:03:40,762
"SO, WHERE'S YOUR BOYFRIEND--
WHAT HIS NAME, CHESTER?"

82
00:03:40,804 --> 00:03:42,639
AND SHE'LL GO,
"NO, IT'S CHANDLER."

83
00:03:42,681 --> 00:03:44,016
AND HE'LL GO, "WHATEVER."

84
00:03:44,058 --> 00:03:45,767
( pained laughter )

85
00:03:46,810 --> 00:03:49,021
THAT-THAT IS
A GOOD TRICK.

86
00:03:50,522 --> 00:03:53,608
ALL RIGHT, LOOK, LOOK,
WHAT AM I GOING TO DO?

87
00:03:53,650 --> 00:03:55,234
LOOK, THEY'RE THERE
TO DO A JOB.

88
00:03:55,276 --> 00:03:56,820
JUST 'CAUSE THEY
WORK TOGETHER

89
00:03:56,862 --> 00:03:58,572
DOESN'T MEAN
THEY'LL GET TOGETHER.

90
00:03:58,613 --> 00:03:59,907
JUST BECAUSE IT HAPPENED

91
00:03:59,948 --> 00:04:01,825
WITH SUSAN SARANDON
AND TIM ROBBINS

92
00:04:01,867 --> 00:04:03,702
DOESN'T MEAN IT'LL
HAPPEN WITH THEM.

93
00:04:03,744 --> 00:04:05,286
OH, OH...

94
00:04:05,328 --> 00:04:08,207
ALEC BALDWIN
AND KIM BASINGER.

95
00:04:08,248 --> 00:04:10,084
OH! TOM CRUISE
AND NICOLE KIDMAN.

96
00:04:10,125 --> 00:04:12,044
YEAH.

97
00:04:12,086 --> 00:04:13,754
MEL GIBSON AND CLINT EASTWOOD.

98
00:04:15,923 --> 00:04:17,257
THEY'RE NOT A COUPLE.

99
00:04:17,298 --> 00:04:19,259
OH, OKAY! I GET THE GAME NOW.

100
00:04:21,178 --> 00:04:22,804
LOOK, LET ME
ASK YOU A QUESTION:

101
00:04:22,846 --> 00:04:24,472
WHEN THEY WERE
DOING IT ON STAGE

102
00:04:24,514 --> 00:04:25,849
WAS IT, LIKE,
REALLY HOT?

103
00:04:25,891 --> 00:04:28,018
OH, YEAH.

104
00:04:28,060 --> 00:04:29,895
WELL, OKAY

105
00:04:29,937 --> 00:04:31,271
SO THEN YOU'RE FINE.

106
00:04:31,312 --> 00:04:32,689
LOOK, THE RULE IS

107
00:04:32,731 --> 00:04:35,776
WHEN TWO ACTORS ARE
ACTUALLY DOING IT OFF STAGE

108
00:04:35,817 --> 00:04:39,404
THEN ALL THE SEXUAL TENSION
BETWEEN THEM IS GONE, OKAY?

109
00:04:39,446 --> 00:04:41,240
SO AS LONG AS
IT'S HOT ON STAGE

110
00:04:41,281 --> 00:04:43,117
YOU GOT NOTHING
TO WORRY ABOUT.

111
00:04:43,158 --> 00:04:44,743
IT'S WHEN THE HEAT
GOES AWAY--

112
00:04:44,785 --> 00:04:46,494
THAT'S WHEN
YOU'RE IN TROUBLE.

113
00:04:47,537 --> 00:04:48,747
REALLY?

114
00:04:48,789 --> 00:04:50,874
YOU HAVE BEEN TO EVERY
PLAY I'VE BEEN IN.

115
00:04:50,916 --> 00:04:52,751
HAVE I EVER HAD CHEMISTRY?
All:
NO.

116
00:04:52,793 --> 00:04:54,502
NO!

117
00:04:58,924 --> 00:05:01,051
SO, MAN, ARE YOU GOING
TO GO SEE THE PLAY

118
00:05:01,093 --> 00:05:02,136
WITH ME TONIGHT?

119
00:05:02,177 --> 00:05:03,929
I DON'T KNOW
HOW COMFORTABLE I AM

120
00:05:03,971 --> 00:05:05,555
GOING TO SEE
HOW HOT THE SEX IS

121
00:05:05,597 --> 00:05:07,557
BETWEEN SOME GUY
AND YOUR GIRLFRIEND.

122
00:05:07,599 --> 00:05:08,934
YEAH, I KNOW, BUT...

123
00:05:08,976 --> 00:05:10,269
NO, NO. OH, I'M THERE.

124
00:05:12,312 --> 00:05:13,772
HEY.
Joey:
HEY, MON.

125
00:05:13,814 --> 00:05:14,773
WANT PANCAKES?

126
00:05:14,815 --> 00:05:16,608
YOU MADE PANCAKES?

127
00:05:16,650 --> 00:05:18,068
YEAH. GRAB A PLATE.

128
00:05:20,028 --> 00:05:21,404
NO, NO. STAY RIGHT THERE.

129
00:05:23,865 --> 00:05:25,784
GETTING CLOSER.

130
00:05:27,161 --> 00:05:28,620
OKAY, OKAY,
BUT DON'T WORRY

131
00:05:28,662 --> 00:05:31,748
BECAUSE WE ALSO HAVE
CEREALS, MUFFINS, WAFFLES

132
00:05:31,790 --> 00:05:33,541
AND JAMS, JELLIES
AND MARMALADES--

133
00:05:33,583 --> 00:05:35,919
WHICH I'M FAIRLY CERTAIN
ARE THE SAME THING.

134
00:05:35,961 --> 00:05:37,504
LISTEN, ALSO,
WE'RE WATCHING

135
00:05:37,545 --> 00:05:40,632
THE GAME HERE SATURDAY NIGHT
IF PEOPLE WANT TO COME OVER.

136
00:05:40,674 --> 00:05:41,883
OH, YEAH.

137
00:05:41,925 --> 00:05:44,136
I WAS THINKING ABOUT
HAVING PEOPLE OVER.

138
00:05:44,178 --> 00:05:46,305
OH, YEAH?
WHO'S PLAYING?

139
00:05:48,140 --> 00:05:49,348
THE PLAYERS.

140
00:05:51,268 --> 00:05:53,145
SOMEBODY SEEMS
TO BE MISSING

141
00:05:53,187 --> 00:05:55,105
BEING THE HOSTESS.

142
00:05:55,147 --> 00:05:56,815
( chuckles ):
PLEASE.

143
00:05:56,857 --> 00:05:58,525
IT'S A RELIEF,
IS WHAT IT IS

144
00:05:58,566 --> 00:06:01,444
IS WHAT IT IS.

145
00:06:01,486 --> 00:06:03,864
PHEEBS, STICK OUT
YOUR PLATE.

146
00:06:10,954 --> 00:06:12,331
MONICA, I'M QUITTING.

147
00:06:12,371 --> 00:06:14,875
I JUST HELPED AN 81-YEAR-OLD
WOMAN PUT ON A THONG

148
00:06:14,916 --> 00:06:16,501
AND SHE DIDN'T EVEN BUY IT.

149
00:06:16,543 --> 00:06:18,295
I'M TELLING YOU, I'M QUITTING.

150
00:06:18,337 --> 00:06:19,546
THAT'S IT.

151
00:06:19,587 --> 00:06:21,131
I'M TALKING TO MY BOSS
RIGHT NOW.

152
00:06:21,173 --> 00:06:22,465
YES, I AM.

153
00:06:22,507 --> 00:06:24,592
YES, I AM. YES, I AM.
YES, I AM. YES, I AM.

154
00:06:24,634 --> 00:06:26,345
CALL ME
WHEN YOU GET THIS MESSAGE.

155
00:06:26,385 --> 00:06:27,888
OH, MR. WALTHAM.

156
00:06:27,929 --> 00:06:30,431
I, UH... REALLY NEED
TO TALK TO YOU.

157
00:06:30,473 --> 00:06:31,683
IN A MOMENT, PLEASE.

158
00:06:31,725 --> 00:06:33,185
I'M IN THE MIDDLE
OF A TASK

159
00:06:33,227 --> 00:06:34,978
AND YOU HAVE A CUSTOMER.

160
00:06:38,273 --> 00:06:39,524
HI.

161
00:06:39,566 --> 00:06:40,984
HI. I'M JOSHUA.

162
00:06:41,026 --> 00:06:42,152
HI. I'M RACHEL GREEN.

163
00:06:42,194 --> 00:06:43,737
WHAT CAN I DO
FOR YOU, JOSHUA?

164
00:06:43,778 --> 00:06:46,281
WELL, I NEED
A WHOLE NEW WARDROBE.

165
00:06:46,323 --> 00:06:48,909
MY WIFE...
WELL, MY EX-WIFE...

166
00:06:48,950 --> 00:06:51,452
OH, I'M SO SORRY.

167
00:06:54,873 --> 00:06:58,252
ANYWAY, SHE BURNED
ALL OF MY CLOTHES.

168
00:06:58,293 --> 00:07:00,795
I GOT AWAY WITH TWO THINGS--
THIS SUIT

169
00:07:00,837 --> 00:07:03,382
AND WHAT TURNED OUT
TO BE A SKIRT.

170
00:07:03,422 --> 00:07:06,551
WELL, AT LEAST
THAT'S A GREAT SUIT.

171
00:07:06,593 --> 00:07:08,553
BUT IT WASN'T MUCH FUN
DROPPING IT OFF

172
00:07:08,595 --> 00:07:10,305
AT THE DRY CLEANERS
IN THE SKIRT.

173
00:07:12,224 --> 00:07:14,059
I NEED EVERYTHING
DOWN TO UNDERWEAR

174
00:07:14,101 --> 00:07:15,269
SO IF YOU'RE WILLING

175
00:07:15,310 --> 00:07:17,271
I'M, UH... I'M ALL YOURS.

176
00:07:17,312 --> 00:07:19,564
OKAY.

177
00:07:19,606 --> 00:07:21,733
RACHEL, YOU NEEDED
TO SPEAK TO ME?

178
00:07:21,775 --> 00:07:24,611
NO, NO,
THAT WASN'T ME.

179
00:07:24,652 --> 00:07:25,946
WELL...

180
00:07:25,987 --> 00:07:27,488
WE SHOULD GET STARTED.

181
00:07:27,530 --> 00:07:29,408
LET ME SHOW YOU MY UNDERWEAR--

182
00:07:31,326 --> 00:07:34,288
THE SELECTION OF UNDERWEAR
THAT WE CARRY.

183
00:07:37,999 --> 00:07:39,167
OH, IT'S THIS WAY.

184
00:07:39,209 --> 00:07:40,294
IT'S THIS WAY.

185
00:07:40,335 --> 00:07:41,420
IT'S THIS WAY?

186
00:07:41,460 --> 00:07:42,587
YEAH.
SORRY.

187
00:07:42,629 --> 00:07:44,131
( sighs )

188
00:07:46,383 --> 00:07:48,009
I'M RIGHT, RIGHT?

189
00:07:48,051 --> 00:07:50,304
THERE WAS, LIKE,
NO CHEMISTRY BETWEEN THEM.

190
00:07:50,345 --> 00:07:51,430
BEFORE THEY HAD HEAT.

191
00:07:51,471 --> 00:07:52,597
NOW THERE'S NO HEAT.

192
00:07:52,639 --> 00:07:54,849
NOW, YOU KNOW
WHAT THIS MEANS.

193
00:07:54,891 --> 00:07:57,018
JOEY TOLD US WHAT THIS MEANS.

194
00:07:57,060 --> 00:07:59,562
ALL RIGHT, LET'S NOT JUMP
TO ANY CONCLUSIONS.

195
00:07:59,604 --> 00:08:02,023
THERE WAS SOME SEXUAL
CHEMISTRY BETWEEN THEM.

196
00:08:02,065 --> 00:08:04,443
COME ON, IT WAS LIKE COUSINS
HAVING SEX.

197
00:08:06,903 --> 00:08:07,946
HERE SHE COMES.

198
00:08:07,988 --> 00:08:09,572
DON'T SAY A WORD.
JUST BE COOL.

199
00:08:09,614 --> 00:08:11,866
DON'T BE, YOU KNOW, YOU.

200
00:08:13,327 --> 00:08:14,786
HEY, YOU GUYS.

201
00:08:14,828 --> 00:08:16,246
HEY.
HEY.

202
00:08:16,288 --> 00:08:18,706
THANK YOU SO MUCH
FOR COMING AGAIN.

203
00:08:18,748 --> 00:08:19,791
DID YOU LIKE IT?

204
00:08:19,833 --> 00:08:20,792
ABSOLUTELY.

205
00:08:20,834 --> 00:08:22,461
MM-HMM.
WASN'T NICK FUNNY

206
00:08:22,501 --> 00:08:24,754
WHEN HE COULDN'T GET
HIS MATCH LIT?

207
00:08:24,796 --> 00:08:27,799
( chuckling stiffly )

208
00:08:29,634 --> 00:08:31,636
IT'S A GOOD PLAY,
ISN'T IT?

209
00:08:31,678 --> 00:08:32,511
MM.

210
00:08:33,388 --> 00:08:34,722
I LOVED THE PLAY.

211
00:08:34,764 --> 00:08:36,224
UH... YEAH,
YOU WERE GREAT

212
00:08:36,266 --> 00:08:38,477
AND NICK-- DITTO.

213
00:08:39,644 --> 00:08:43,357
CLEARLY, YOU'RE
HAVING SEX WITH HIM.

214
00:08:45,150 --> 00:08:47,194
OKAY...

215
00:08:50,613 --> 00:08:53,492
CLEARLY, I'M HAVING
SEX WITH HIM?

216
00:08:53,533 --> 00:08:54,617
IT WAS SO OBVIOUS!

217
00:08:54,659 --> 00:08:56,495
THERE WAS NO CHEMISTRY
BETWEEN YOU.

218
00:08:56,536 --> 00:08:58,663
OKAY, LET ME
JUST GET THIS STRAIGHT:

219
00:08:58,705 --> 00:09:00,874
YOU'RE ACCUSING ME
OF CHEATING ON YOU

220
00:09:00,915 --> 00:09:03,251
AND YOU'RE INSULTING
MY PERFORMANCE?

221
00:09:03,293 --> 00:09:04,919
I CAN SEE HOW
THIS COULD HAPPEN.

222
00:09:04,961 --> 00:09:06,838
YOU KNOW, YOU'RE
UP THERE EVERY NIGHT

223
00:09:06,880 --> 00:09:08,256
NAKED, TOUCHING,
KISSING.

224
00:09:08,298 --> 00:09:09,883
ACTING.

225
00:09:09,924 --> 00:09:11,592
CHANDLER,
THIS IS MY JOB.

226
00:09:11,634 --> 00:09:13,678
I-I'M PLAYING
A PART IN A PLAY.

227
00:09:13,720 --> 00:09:15,180
HOW CAN YOU
NOT TRUST ME?

228
00:09:15,222 --> 00:09:18,683
WELL, YOU CAN UNDERSTAND,
GIVEN HOW WE STARTED.

229
00:09:18,725 --> 00:09:20,101
OH, WOW.

230
00:09:20,143 --> 00:09:22,645
I CAN'T BELIEVE YOU'RE
THROWING THAT IN MY FACE.

231
00:09:22,687 --> 00:09:23,855
THAT IS WHAT HAPPENED

232
00:09:23,897 --> 00:09:25,899
AND I DON'T EVEN SEE YOU
DENYING THIS.

233
00:09:25,940 --> 00:09:27,734
I'LL TELL YOU WHAT,
CHANDLER.

234
00:09:27,775 --> 00:09:29,986
WHY DON'T YOU CALL ME
WHEN YOU GROW UP?

235
00:09:30,028 --> 00:09:31,279
YEAH, WELL

236
00:09:31,321 --> 00:09:33,865
DON'T EXPECT THAT
TO HAPPEN ANYTIME SOON.

237
00:09:38,245 --> 00:09:40,788
OH! I HAVE THE BEST JOB
IN THE ENTIRE WORLD.

238
00:09:40,830 --> 00:09:42,957
THE MOST ADORABLE GUY
CAME OVER TODAY

239
00:09:42,999 --> 00:09:46,627
AND I GOT
TO DRESS HIM UP ALL DAY.

240
00:09:46,669 --> 00:09:49,256
